# Career Alert Digest — 2026-10-10

## Faculty Job Postings
- [Assistant Professor, Transportation Engineering, University of Nebraska-Lincoln](https://jobs.nebraska.edu/UniversityNebraskaSystem/job/Assistant-Professor-Transportation-Engineering/1463-en_US) — TT line in CEE, Omaha-based with teaching across both campuses, expects an externally-funded research program. Deadline: rolling/none listed, Aug 2026 start.
- [Assistant/Associate Professor, Transportation Engineering, Missouri S&T (CArEE)](https://www.pharmadiversityjobboard.com/job/assistant-associate-professor-civil-architectural-and-environmental-engineering-00096512) — Open to any transportation systems area incl. CAV/shared/electric vehicles, mobility, digital twins — strong match for CAV + AI/ML hot topics. Deadline: not listed, fall 2026 start.
- [Assistant Professor, Transportation Engineering, The College of New Jersey](https://careers.insidehighered.com/job/3553088/assistant-professor-civil-engineering/) — Transportation systems analysis, planning, data-informed decision making; teacher-scholar model. Deadline: not listed, Fall 2027 start (term 08/07/2027–06/07/2030).
- [Tenure-Track Faculty, Transportation Engineering, Marquette University](https://employment.marquette.edu/postings/23696) — Transportation + data analytics/AI knowledge a plus; associate-level candidates also considered. Deadline: not listed; verify posting is still active before applying. Aug 2026 start.
- [Multiple TT Faculty Positions (Geosystems & Transportation Systems Engineering), Georgia Tech CEE — Job ID 304458](https://careers.insidehighered.com/job/3559016/multiple-tenure-track-faculty-positions-in-civil-and-environmental-engineering/) — New TSE-specific search (distinct from the previously tracked 2024-25 search, Job 277821); all ranks, preference for Assistant Professor. Deadline: not listed/rolling.

## Conference Deadlines / CFPs
- [TRB 2027 Annual Meeting — Paper Submissions](https://www.nationalacademies.org/events/887) — Jan 10–14, 2027, Washington DC; paper submission site opens July 1 and closes Aug 1, 2027; new format requires structured abstract in-paper, 20-page max, Chicago author-date refs. Deadline: Aug 1, 2027.

## Journal Special Issue CFPs
- [Transportation Research Part D — "AI-Driven Modelling and Enhancement for Transportation Resilience under Disasters"](https://servicesetu.org/call-for-paper/journals/trte) — Matches resilience/climate + AI/ML hot topics; covers pre-event vulnerability prediction, post-event assessment, adaptive emergency response. Deadline: Feb 12, 2027. (Could not confirm on elsevier.com directly — verify on the journal's Editorial Manager page before submitting.)
- [Tri-continental Special Issue — "Informal and Shared Mobility" (Transportation Research Interdisciplinary Perspectives / Asian, African & Latin American Transport Studies)](https://vref.se/other/2026/new-call-for-papers-on-informal-and-shared-mobility/) — Matches shared mobility + equity hot topics; tied to the First Global Convening on Informal and Shared Mobility, Bangkok, Oct 26–28, 2026 — can submit without attending. Deadline: not confirmed in search results; conference is only ~2 weeks out, so check the full CFP PDF immediately if interested.

